<SddDeviationReview keywords="deviation, final, batch, audit, operator" type="directive" ver="1.0">
  <Mission>
    Review disputed autonomous decisions once, after the whole batch is complete. This is a dynamic
    final conversation over durable owner logs and completed audit evidence. It creates no sidecar;
    it resolves each item by editing that existing Decision Log record through the canonical CLI.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-stateless-flow"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <Contracts>
    {{> "contract/process/deviation-record-format"}}
    {{> "contract/process/question-rule-slim"}}
  </Contracts>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_1_COLLECT">
      <Goal>Build the bounded final review set.</Goal>
      <Action>
        From the completed batch's exact artifact paths, collect only its Decision Log entries and
        Execution Log Handoff deviations recorded per `DEVIATION_RECORD_FORMAT`. Add the audit findings
        returned for this batch. Per `AX_STATELESS_FLOW`, do not search unrelated history or
        reconstruct transcript memory.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_2_REVIEW">
      <Goal>Resolve every exceptional choice with the operator.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Present three compact lists: `Deviations` (what, why, where, source), `Audit findings`
        (severity, evidence, owner), and `Questions` (one concrete accept/correct question for each
        unresolved item). If all three are empty, say so and finish without a ceremony. Otherwise ask
        once for the operator's decisions. Route corrections to their existing artifact owner and
        invalidate the applicable approval marker; never patch code from this review directive.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_PERSIST">
      <Goal>Persist every operator verdict on its existing deviation record.</Goal>
      <Action>
        For each reviewed record call <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="verdictWrite">npx gennady sdd-log &lt;ticket&gt; deviation-verdict &lt;D-id&gt; &lt;accepted|rework|rolled-back&gt;</ToolCall>
        Inputs &lt;ticket&gt;, &lt;D-id&gt;, &lt;accepted|rework|rolled-back&gt;: the exact reviewed ticket,
        existing Decision Log identity, and operator-selected closed verdict. Use verdictWrite.
        `rework` routes through `AX_REOPEN_FORMAT`; `rolled-back` identifies the superseding Decision
        Log fact in the record prose. Never create a sidecar or append a duplicate deviation. Then run
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="integrityCheck">npx gennady sdd-check --all .</ToolCall>
        and use integrityCheck; finish only when it carries no `SDD_DEVIATION_VERDICT_MISSING`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>
</SddDeviationReview>
